<%
// PRJEDU_pages: what a page may see. A page runs with the VISITOR's role:
// Guest (0) before a login, the user's role after one (login.ayp).
// MNT_CODE's xdb_acl gives every right to Engineer (6) and Admin (7) and
// nothing below, so it reads as empty for a Guest and for an Operator -
// while a script of the engine itself (role 9, System) reads it fine:
// start() could log it. The set points' xdb_acl lets everyone read them
// and only Operator and up write them.
var title = "Access";
var refresh = 0;
var code = evt.GetValue("id('MNT_CODE')/@val");
var lvl = evt.GetValue("id('T1_LVL')/@val");
var hi = evt.GetValue("id('T1_SP_HI')/@val");
-%>
<%@ include file="part/head.ayp" %>
<h1>What this page may read</h1>
<table>
  <tr><th>Value</th><th>xdb_acl</th><th>Read by this page</th></tr>
  <tr><td>T1_LVL</td><td>(none: open)</td><td><%= lvl %></td></tr>
  <tr><td>T1_SP_HI</td><td>0x33333111 (read for every role, write from Operator)</td><td><%= hi %></td></tr>
  <tr><td>MNT_CODE</td><td>0xFF000000 (Engineer and Admin only)</td>
      <td><%= code == null ? "(nothing - not readable for this visitor)" : code %></td></tr>
</table>
<p>You are <b><%= ses.user == "" ? "not logged in (Guest)" : ses.user %></b>, role <b><%= ses.user_role %></b>.
A page is not a back door: it reads and writes with the rights of whoever asked for it,
through the same xdb_acl as MQTT, MCP and the telnet shell (docs/06_Access_and_Safety.md).
<% if (ses.user == "") { -%><a href="/login.ayp?next=/access.ayp">Log in</a> as opr, then as eng, and watch this table.<% } -%></p>
<%@ include file="part/foot.ayp" %>
